{"file":"Token Shield-1.8.0-v2.zip","bytes":974981,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"token-shield","description":"A playbook skill that cuts Claude Code token spend: sourced prompt cache rules, session boundary decisions, model tier routing, plugin and MCP pruning, output discipline, and a durable-memory pattern. Ships opt-in tools that read the API usage counters from local transcripts: a measurement script, a context linter, a session telemetry hook, a deterministic advisor that ranks your next best move, and a Token Shield dashboard. Every claim is documented with the check that backs it.","version":"1.8.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/khalilmaaouni/token-shield","keywords":["tokens","cost","prompt-caching","compaction","model-routing","context-window"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/token-shield/SKILL.md","name":"token-shield","description":"Cut Claude Code token spend without cutting quality. This skill should be used when the work involves prompt caching (cache writes, cache hits, TTL, refreshes), deciding between /rewind, /compact, /clear and a fresh session, routing work to the right model tier, pruning plugins and MCP servers that clog the context window, reducing verbose output, or auditing what a session costs. Triggers include tokens, cost, cache, caching, compact, compaction, context full, expensive, spend, budget, token economy, prune plugins.","headings":["Token Shield","The cost model","Measure before you optimize","Lever 1: keep the cache hot","Lever 2: shrink the always-loaded context","Lever 3: choose the right session boundary","Lever 4: route the model to the job","Lever 5: output discipline","Lever 6: durable memory beats re-derivation","Anti-pattern ledger","The sibling bill: cloud metered usage","Machine-local overlay"],"name_hint":"变量/Token · shield","description_zh":"优化 Claude Code 的令牌使用，涵盖提示缓存、TTL、刷新、/rewind／compact／clear或新会话选择、模型档位、插件与 MCP 精简、输出长度及会话成本审计。"}],"commands":[{"path":"comman